  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TVET digitization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Facilitate research on market trends assessment, identifying current supply/demand in TVET and ensuring job placement opportunities as well as feasibility of digital training delivery

- Facilitate field testing of application through customer reach piloting among the existing youth group networks from empower youth for work (EYW project) and Reecall project (oxfam&#x2019;s flagship programme) where Oxfam has around 400+ youth groups and 6000 youths.

- Help enhance partnership for TVET app developers by organizing peer networking sessions for infrastructural, equity, and advisory.

- Coordinate with Top content makers and TVET graduates (Heroes of our platform) to run campaigns promoting the platform itself.

- Policy  discussions will be held with different stakeholders like
o   Government departments to discuss scope of integration with existing TVET framework, scope of inclusion and empowerment of marginalized population, scope of inclusion of outbound migrants/remittance earners
o   Regional and global skill development networks to set thefoundation for integration of new age technology like AI, new management practices based on data. Further technical and financial will also be gathered when necessary and possible

- Develop policy briefs on TVET digitalization and conduct advocacy campaign by engaging A2i, youth ministry, ministry of education, thinks tanks (CPD) and ICT divisions.

- Communication efforts will be undertakento disseminate the knowledge gathered during the project through
o   Learning reflection workshops and round tables with relevant stakeholders
o   Internal channels of Oxfam

- Facilitate conduction of impact measurement study</narrative>
  </description>
